"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P,Q,P_0,Q_0,\\leq_P,\\leq_Q,\\mathbb P,\\mathbb Q,\\tau_P,\\tau_Q,A,B,f\\in V\">\\(P,Q,P_0,Q_0,\\leq_P,\\leq_Q,\\mathbb P,\\mathbb Q,\\tau_P,\\tau_Q,A,B,f\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Poset}:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Poset}:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"d3f859dbdd37f018\" href=\"?note=d3f859dbdd37f018\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-poset.md\">../batch02/58-df-poset.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{TopologicalSpace}_S\\subseteq V^2\">\\(\\operatorname{TopologicalSpace}_S\\subseteq V^2\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Bijective}\\subseteq V^3\">\\(\\mathrm{Bijective}\\subseteq V^3\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcForcing10ForcingEquivalence}_S,\\mathrm{ZfcForcing5ForcingEquivalence}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcForcing10ForcingEquivalence}_S,\\mathrm{ZfcForcing5ForcingEquivalence}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}forcing10\\text{-}forcing\\text{-}equivalence}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcForcing10ForcingEquivalence}_S(P,Q)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\leftrightarrow\\exists P_0,Q_0,\\leq_P,\\leq_Q,\\tau_P,\\tau_Q,A,B,f\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\nP=\\langle P_0,\\leq_P\\rangle\\land Q=\\langle Q_0,\\leq_Q\\rangle\n\\land\\mathrm{Poset}(P_0,\\leq_P)\\land\\mathrm{Poset}(Q_0,\\leq_Q)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\tau_P=\\{U\\subseteq P_0:\\forall p\\in U\\;\\forall q\\in P_0\\;(\n\\langle q,p\\rangle\\in\\leq_P\\to q\\in U)\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\tau_Q=\\{U\\subseteq Q_0:\\forall p\\in U\\;\\forall q\\in Q_0\\;(\n\\langle q,p\\rangle\\in\\leq_Q\\to q\\in U)\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\operatorname{TopologicalSpace}_S(P_0,\\tau_P)\n\\land\\operatorname{TopologicalSpace}_S(Q_0,\\tau_Q)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land A=\\{U\\in\\tau_P:U=\\operatorname{int}_{\\tau_P}(\\operatorname{cl}_{\\tau_P}(U))\\}\n\\land B=\\{U\\in\\tau_Q:U=\\operatorname{int}_{\\tau_Q}(\\operatorname{cl}_{\\tau_Q}(U))\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\mathrm{Bijective}(f,A,B)\n\\land\\forall U,V\\in A\\;(f(U\\cap V)=f(U)\\cap f(V))\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\forall U\\in A\\;\\Bigl(\nf(\\operatorname{int}_{\\tau_P}(P_0\\setminus U))\n=\\operatorname{int}_{\\tau_Q}(Q_0\\setminus f(U))\\Bigr)\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}forcing10\\text{-}forcing\\text{-}equivalence}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcForcing10ForcingEquivalence}_S(P,Q)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\leftrightarrow\\exists P_0,Q_0,\\leq_P,\\leq_Q,\\tau_P,\\tau_Q,A,B,f\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\nP=\\langle P_0,\\leq_P\\rangle\\land Q=\\langle Q_0,\\leq_Q\\rangle\n\\land\\mathrm{Poset}(P_0,\\leq_P)\\land\\mathrm{Poset}(Q_0,\\leq_Q)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\tau_P=\\{U\\subseteq P_0:\\forall p\\in U\\;\\forall q\\in P_0\\;(\n\\langle q,p\\rangle\\in\\leq_P\\to q\\in U)\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\tau_Q=\\{U\\subseteq Q_0:\\forall p\\in U\\;\\forall q\\in Q_0\\;(\n\\langle q,p\\rangle\\in\\leq_Q\\to q\\in U)\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\operatorname{TopologicalSpace}_S(P_0,\\tau_P)\n\\land\\operatorname{TopologicalSpace}_S(Q_0,\\tau_Q)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land A=\\{U\\in\\tau_P:U=\\operatorname{int}_{\\tau_P}(\\operatorname{cl}_{\\tau_P}(U))\\}\n\\land B=\\{U\\in\\tau_Q:U=\\operatorname{int}_{\\tau_Q}(\\operatorname{cl}_{\\tau_Q}(U))\\}\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\mathrm{Bijective}(f,A,B)\n\\land\\forall U,V\\in A\\;(f(U\\cap V)=f(U)\\cap f(V))\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\forall U\\in A\\;\\Bigl(\nf(\\operatorname{int}_{\\tau_P}(P_0\\setminus U))\n=\\operatorname{int}_{\\tau_Q}(Q_0\\setminus f(U))\\Bigr)\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}forcing10\\text{-}forcing\\text{-}equivalence} \\vdash \\mathrm{ZfcForcing5ForcingEquivalence}_S(\\mathbb P,\\mathbb Q)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{ZfcForcing10ForcingEquivalence}_S(\\mathbb P,\\mathbb Q)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}forcing10\\text{-}forcing\\text{-}equivalence} \\vdash \\mathrm{ZfcForcing5ForcingEquivalence}_S(\\mathbb P,\\mathbb Q)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{ZfcForcing10ForcingEquivalence}_S(\\mathbb P,\\mathbb Q)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Forcing equivalence is expressed as a Boolean-algebra isomorphism between the two regular-open completions. The formula constructs their carriers and preserves meet and regular-open complement directly, rather than passing bare carrier sets to the model-theoretic structure-isomorphism predicate.</li>\n<li><code>58-df-zfc-forcing5-forcing-equivalence</code> is merged here; both definitions use regular-open algebra isomorphism.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md","status":"resolved","id":"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch02/58-df-poset.md","status":"resolved","id":"d3f859dbdd37f018","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-df-poset.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch12/58-df-topological-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"815e63e5071e7b58","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · de